WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:06.840
In previous lessons we looked at nonhomogeneous
systems of linear equations. In them

2
00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:13.640
the constant terms usually stand on the right,
and at least one of them is nonzero.

3
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:19.360
In this lesson we will look at solving
homogeneous systems of linear equations.

4
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:27.580
If all the constant terms are zero, the system
of equations is called homogeneous.

5
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:32.760
The Kronecker–Capelli theorem implies that it
is always consistent.

6
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.090
If the rank of the matrix equals the number of
unknowns,

7
00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:43.390
